     "content": "Slow down, you are on island time",
     "locked": false,
     "editable": true,
     "zIndex": 1
    },
    {
     "id": "e144",
     "type": "article",
     "frame": {
      "x": 40,
      "y": 150,
      "width": 515,
      "height": 380
     },
     "x": 40,
     "y": 150,
     "w": 515,
     "h": 380,
     "transform": {
      "rotation": 0,
      "scaleX": 1,
      "scaleY": 1,
      "opacity": 1
     },
     "style": {
      "fontSize": 12.5,
      "color": "#334155",
      "lineHeight": 1.55
     },
     "content": "There is a particular rhythm to life on the islands. Mornings start with kava and conversation, afternoons stretch out under the shade of a breadfruit tree, and evenings belong to the tide.\n\nThis issue is an invitation to travel that way: unhurried, curious and connected to the people who call these places home. We visit villages that welcome visitors with a sevusevu, taste recipes passed down through generations and find the quiet corners that guidebooks miss.\n\nWherever you read this, we hope it sends you somewhere beautiful.",
     "locked": false,
     "editable": true,
